{"acceptedClaimRefs":[{"assessmentDigest":"sha256:cc7dbe3937f164d8f6e533d343a02d66f1e5bb4592a924001d13af9fdf0d3798","claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-product-code-quotient-local-maximum","judgmentId":"sha256:ebee9dfee81fa760589e21f275573709beab85fe319c0deab2dbcc7b26423370","transactionId":"9ff49a7c2d1c242d6cb29cf9afd34803b06d2383"}],"acceptedClaims":[{"claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/two-letter-marton-product-code-quotient-local-maximum","dependencyTransactionIds":["88a1004f309460f3ec1cacdae88d30f88559f9bc"],"statement":"For the governed two-use half-skew BSSC, fix W and X^2 to four symbols and the four deterministic product-code orientations (U,V)=(X^2,0),(2X_1,X_2),(X_2,2X_1),(0,X^2), and vary only the 16 positive masses q(W,X^2). At the tensor product of the exact one-use RTD optimizer, whose 4x4 mass matrix has entries (11-sqrt(105))/120, 1/30, and (11+sqrt(105))/120 in the displayed symmetry pattern, the half-weight Marton functional L_{1/2} has constant gradient and a negative-definite Hessian on the full 15-dimensional simplex tangent space. A standard-library checker works exactly in Q(sqrt(105)), verifies all 15 gradient log-product identities, and gives an exact LDL^T decomposition with 15 strictly negative pivots and exact reconstruction. Hence this tensor point is a strict local maximum in the stated fixed-map quotient; its value is 2 L_RTD, and every distinct sufficiently close law in this quotient has selected-law Marton value below 2 L_RTD because min(E_Y,E_Z) <= L_{1/2}. This local theorem does not rule out distant points, directions activating other (W,U,V,X^2) atoms, stochastic or different maps, larger auxiliaries, a two-letter Marton gain in another architecture, Marton additivity, or a capacity converse."}],"evidenceChunkDigests":["sha256:0838e33e076c5713cadd26ca23255dcf9d1f446df4652b16c3f42612c3445036","sha256:9764fcc6d169eaa82f04d483f6dec405c8df5eff3f9c94bcee3dd46a1ee40b69","sha256:c016a6c6689e6f8b8a600e75aebc70c441e282f78187e31c51d